<title>UK: BICC gets nod for North Durham hospital.</title>
<headline>BICC gets nod for North Durham hospital.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>British engineering and construction group BICC Plc said on Friday a consortium of which it was part had been given government approval to complete negotiations for a 65 million stg new North Durham hospital.  </p>
<p>Consort Healthcare is made up of BICC and the Royal Bank of Scotland Plc.</p>
<p>Construction of the 454-bed hospital will be carried out by BICC subsidiaries Balfour Beatty Construction and Haden Young. Finance for the project will be provided by Royal Bank of Scotland, in conjunction with a group of banks.</p>
<p>BICC announced last week that the consortium had been given approval to complete negotiations for a 180 million stg new Royal Infirmary and University Medical School in Edinburgh.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 4019</p>
</text>
